{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7QfnvpXWg9NGDBFw9cR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## The angle\n\nInvestors will work out the runway as soon as they see the numbers: $480k ÷ $44k ≈ **11 months**, with revenue flat. They haven't heard from you in six months, so their first worry will be whether you see that and have a plan. The update should answer it.\n\nThe story that holds together is this: **we lost our biggest customer to a scheduler built into their electronic records system, and that showed us both the threat and the part of our product that survives it.** A records system can bundle a calendar. It's much harder for it to match your reminder results. That's why reminders-only for $150 a month is the right next move, and it makes the launch your strategy rather than one item on a list. The update should read as \"here's what happened, what we learned, and what we're doing about it,\" not as \"flat quarter, but here's some good news.\"\n\n## Order\n\n1. **Start with the hard numbers.** MRR flat at $41k, the biggest customer gone, about 11 months of runway. Acknowledge the missed updates in one sentence and commit to quarterly from now on. Don't over-apologize.\n2. **Why the customer left.** Say it was their records system's built-in scheduler. Then say honestly how many of your remaining customers face the same risk.\n3. **What held up.** Gross adds were good: replacing $5.5k of lost revenue is real sales work. The reminder result is the main evidence: no-shows fell from 13% to 7%.\n4. **The plan.** Reminders-only launches next month at $150. Give a specific target for the next update, such as X paying clinics by a certain date.\n5. **Cash.** Say what you'll do: raise, cut, or a path to break-even, with dates. A vague answer here will hurt you more than any other number.\n6. **Asks.** Make them specific: introductions to multi-site physical therapy groups, contacts at records-system companies, help with fundraising.\n\n## Leave out\n\n- Long explanations for the missed updates.\n- \"We added 9 clinics!\" on its own. It looks like spin without the churn next to it.\n- The departed chain's name.\n- Roadmap or team detail that has nothing to do with the plan above.\n\n## Find out before writing\n\n- **Clinics or customers?** The 12-clinic chain is \"one of the 4\" you lost, so you must be counting customers there. Count the same way throughout, or investors will catch it.\n- **MRR at your last update** and what you promised then. They'll compare.\n- **Is $44k net burn or gross spending?** Will you cut costs, and when?\n- **How solid is the 7% vs 13%?** How many clinics, over what period? Is it a before/after comparison that seasonality could explain?\n- **Dollar value.** Each point of no-show reduction is worth so many missed visits times the value of a visit. If one clinic saves well over $150 a month, lead with that number.\n- **Can reminders-only work with clinics' existing schedulers?** Which records systems does it connect to today?\n- **Demand signals.** Do you have a waitlist, pilots, or letters of intent? Would the chain that left buy reminders-only? Call them. A yes from them would be your strongest sentence.\n- **Risk of downgrades.** What do current customers pay on average? Could some switch down to the $150 tier?\n- **Concentration.** What share of MRR comes from your largest remaining customer?\n- **The fundraising decision.** Make it before writing. The update can't be vague about cash.\n\nFinally, consider calling your two or three biggest investors before you send it. After a six-month silence, they shouldn't learn about the lost customer and the 11-month runway from a group email."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5315,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5315},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a94c79e-a094-4535-8b2c-c7b33e3f9f53","uuid":"c9acadb4-f45f-4900-b08a-1ea25d73612f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T22:38:49.988Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7QfnnszeGDM6i4vP8Md"}
